# What NetSurf may NAME. The other half is nsemblink.caps, which says what it
# may DO; the kernel enforces both, and a grant here can only ever narrow what
# the session already holds.
#
# It reads three things and writes nothing: the OS's font, NetSurf's own
# resources (its user-agent stylesheet -- a page never finishes loading
# without them), and whatever documents ship with the system. Everything else
# it renders arrives over the network and is never written down, because this
# port has no cookie jar and no cache on disk yet.

ro /system                  # the font, netsurf's resources, /system/web
